NAME
    find - recursively list files and directories

SYNOPSIS
    find [path] [-name pattern]

DESCRIPTION
    Walks <path> (default: current directory) and everything under it,
    printing one entry per line, each path shown relative the same way it
    was given (e.g. 'find EmuSen' prints 'EmuSen/...' paths). -name filters
    to entries whose own name matches a glob ('*'/'?' wildcards only, no
    regex) - a directory that doesn't match is still walked into, only
    excluded from the printed list itself, matching real find's own
    behavior. Walled to the project's own directory tree (see 'cd').

EXAMPLES
    find
    find EmuSen.DianaSh -name '*Command.cs'
